(7408933, 1167212, 38032, '<td valign="top">As far as interpreting this piece as an artwork at Dismaland, I''m sure there could be many opinions.<br/>To me, it is reminiscent of the haunted house ride at Disney, where you see yourself in mirrors sitting next to ghosts - but instead of moving through a ride, here you sit - likely unconcerned for the humorous yet horrific event right nearby. Possibly a metaphor for how we tend to separate ourselves from that which we don''t want to see.  This seems to be set up as a photo studio of sorts; truly an impressive interpretive piece that allows for immediate interaction from the visitors. <br/>Congrats on the ribbon and accolades.</td>', 'As far as interpreting this piece as an artwork at Dismaland, I''m sure there could be many opinions.To me, it is reminiscent of the haunted house ride at Disney, where you see yourself in mirrors sitting next to ghosts - but instead of moving through a ride, here you sit - likely unconcerned for the humorous yet horrific event right nearby. Possibly a metaphor for how we tend to separate ourselves from that which we don''t want to see.  This seems to be set up as a photo studio of sorts; truly an impressive interpretive piece that allows for immediate interaction from the visitors. Congrats on the ribbon and accolades.', '2015-10-08 09:17:09.000000', NULL, 0),
